{"id": "EUVD-2026-103696", "enisaUuid": "9c04b2da-7dc6-3204-9a5d-bd8f28c928ae", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: mgmt: fix race in read_unconf_index_list()\n\nread_unconf_index_list() counts unconfigured controllers before allocating\nits response, then checks the device flags again while filling it.\n\nhci_dev_list_lock stabilizes list membership, but it does not serialize the\nper-device flags. During asynchronous controller setup, the worker can set\nHCI_UNCONFIGURED and clear HCI_SETUP between the two passes. A controller\nomitted from the allocation count can then become eligible for the fill\npass, causing an out-of-bounds write to rp->index[].\n\nAllocate space for every device on hci_dev_list. Since list membership\ncannot change while hci_dev_list_lock is held, the response remains large\nenough regardless of flag transitions. The reported count and response\nlength still include only eligible unconfigured controllers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/524e0450dd9a396f99a81b045219b0e2ea0dab57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ddf962c76432a10a6cb80042875cbc48a9c056b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/416546cd6a54e9b68f2b91bc680b1ee17dcd77a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e8bba0360d1379bfa8da47c8f5dadbb10a3fba1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5dbb41b212c50c095a4dbee3017a84fe94f033b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-79jp-j4mv-p57c", "CVE-2026-98456"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2791627b-1366-39f7-8b03-d09815b1003a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "4a109a5b-26cf-334c-b71d-b53cac5f4210", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "73d1df2a7a1036a1f000e5f0ece6ade3e082b854 <416546cd6a54e9b68f2b91bc680b1ee17dcd77a1"}, {"id": "4e79eb7b-b14a-34b9-88b4-5e15c7e5c265", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "7ffdf078-b1b2-31e9-8d14-830fd40a3192", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "843131d4-2768-3548-b5cf-44e2a5b4318e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.17"}, {"id": "a00a037d-b57b-35eb-8bbf-48c17eb50ca0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "a896e41c-979f-396f-b980-5a048f949237", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "73d1df2a7a1036a1f000e5f0ece6ade3e082b854 <8ddf962c76432a10a6cb80042875cbc48a9c056b"}, {"id": "a986502c-7111-3e4c-b064-973a53de1d5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "73d1df2a7a1036a1f000e5f0ece6ade3e082b854 <524e0450dd9a396f99a81b045219b0e2ea0dab57"}, {"id": "cff8ace4-7be8-31fe-8db7-8b1a4017be40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "73d1df2a7a1036a1f000e5f0ece6ade3e082b854 <2e8bba0360d1379bfa8da47c8f5dadbb10a3fba1"}, {"id": "de04a408-a1a8-3113-954c-0337312451d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e4738b78-9f37-3ae9-b1a8-cdb21d467ee7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "f971c586-570b-3c4b-ba8e-86eafc91bb7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "73d1df2a7a1036a1f000e5f0ece6ade3e082b854 <b5dbb41b212c50c095a4dbee3017a84fe94f033b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f2b4350b-b305-3d96-9981-8fe613f0d075", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}